      "body": "### Preflight Checklist\n\n- [X] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\n- [X] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\n- [X] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a feature request that matches the one I want to file, without success.\n\n### Problem Description\n\nI am writing a mouse/keyboard sharing application in Electron. I would like the ability to hide the mouse pointer when the pointer is \"off screen\" on another computer.\r\n\r\nI found a [similar question](https://github.com/electron/electron/issues/17889) that linked to an [MDN article](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Pointer_Lock_API), but the [example code](https://github.com/mdn/dom-examples/tree/main/pointer-lock) does not work in Electron.\n\n### Proposed Solution\n\nProvide native control over the OS mouse.\n\n### Alternatives Considered\n\nI have tried using [robot.js](http://robotjs.io/) to bury the mouse outside of screen coordinates but this is not working properly. The mouse is still visible.\n\n### Additional Information\n\n_No response_",
